{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"dc915aa5-562a-4d40-ab12-39bf546dd9ee","agentId":"acbfb63ee5bb37cdd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"No subagents/forks, no commits/pushes, no searching, no screenshots (memory is low). Token-efficient; 3 checks; report under 60 words. Files only: cuore/services/experience_bridge.py, cuore/web/templates/_experience.html, cuore/tests/check_experience_page.py. Do not edit cuore.css (use existing classes: .card-details, .chip, .btn, .small, .muted).\n\nRepo C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers; Python .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe. In experience_bridge.links_for(...): compute a `score` per link and sort by it: relevance (matched by exact code 100, family 60, job 40; vehicle_fit exact model +30, sibling +10, generic 0) then importance (reputation high +20, medium +10; kind how_to_video +15, teardown +12, forum_thread +10, owner_report +5, sound_reference +8; recency: +1 per year since 2020, cap 6). Return `reason` per link (e.g. \"exact code, this model, hands-on video\") and keep the merged/deduplicated result. In _experience.html: render as a collapsed `<details class=\"card-details\">` whose summary reads \"Others' experience (N)\" with the top link's title as a teaser; inside, a form-free `<select>` is not possible without JS, so provide view links `?exp=relevant|videos|forums|newest` (the template reads `request.query_params.get('exp')` if `request` is defined, else \"relevant\") that filter/sort client-side-free by rendering the already-sorted list and hiding non-matching kinds with plain Jinja conditions; each row shows rank number, kind icon text, title (external, rel=noopener), source and date, the `reason` in small muted text, reputation chip. Checks: links_for returns descending scores with an exact-code video first; the rendered section is collapsed by default with \"(N)\" in the summary; ?exp=forums shows only forum threads. Run check_experience_page.py."},"uuid":"1faf23df-d694-43d2-a87b-a63918959c49",