{"parentUuid":"167b0e51-1b5b-49b3-b489-1636a5bf3172","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"acbfb63ee5bb37cdd","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfpiEhLpk6QEmttS38PVd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CTjRAiY76p4SetYYtQDqAn","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\mes-log-mcp\\mes\\platform.py"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1315,"cache_read_input_tokens":69085,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1315,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":14,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01CTjRAiY76p4SetYYtQDqAn":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\mes-log-mcp\\mes\\platform.py"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"d1e8d585-4d70-4988-a65b-d41272e1d3e6","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfpiEh4y4vx6vqbAjrDqx","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"9efdfdf4-685d-475b-8aa9-7f640e7535cf","timestamp":"2026-10-08T11:44:08.480Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"9efdfdf4-685d-475b-8aa9-7f640e7535cf","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"dc915aa5-562a-4d40-ab12-39bf546dd9ee","agentId":"acbfb63ee5bb37cdd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CTjRAiY76p4SetYYtQDqAn","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Platform relationships between this project's car and its \"similar\"\n2\tStellantis/Maserati siblings.\n3\t\n4\tThe user has described the 2018 Alfa Romeo Stelvio 2.0T's two \"similar\"\n5\tsibling cars as the Maserati Levante and the Maserati Grecale. House rule\n6\t(see ``feedback_...`` memory): never present an unverified relationship as\n7\tfact. This module is a small, sourced table of what is actually shared\n8\tbetween these cars' platforms -- and, just as importantly, what is NOT --\n9\tso the rest of the project (``mes.experience``, ``mes.parts``,\n10\t``mes.code_feel`` and their ``cuore`` bridges) can label a sibling-platform\n11\tresult \"verify fit\" instead of presenting it as settled.\n12\t\n13\tConfidence levels (never invented -- an absent/unverified relationship is\n14\trecorded as UNKNOWN, never guessed):\n15\t\n16\t* ``CONFIRMED``     -- stated directly by a primary source (the\n17\t                       manufacturer's own platform article/spec sheet).\n18\t* ``CORROBORATED``  -- two independent sources agree (e.g. Wikipedia's\n19\t                       Grecale article plus the FCA Global Medium Engine\n20\t                       article both naming the same shared engine family).\n21\t* ``SINGLE_SOURCE``  -- exactly one source found, not cross-checked.\n22\t* ``UNKNOWN``       -- nothing credible found, or the two cars are\n23\t                       confirmed to NOT share the thing being asked about\n24\t                       (e.g. Levante and Stelvio do not share a platform).\n25\t\n26\tResearch pass: 2026-10-07, via web search + page fetch of:\n27\t\n28\t* https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maserati_Grecale -- \"the Grecale shares the\n29\t  company's Giorgio platform with the Alfa Romeo Stelvio and the fifth\n30\t  generation Jeep Grand Cherokee.\"\n31\t* https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FCA_Global_Medium_Engine -- the GME T4 2.0L\n32\t  turbo engine family, first fitted to the Giulia/Stelvio, also used in the\n33\t  Grecale.\n34\t* https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfa_Romeo_Stelvio -- Giorgio platform,\n35\t  ZF 8HP50 (base/Ti) / ZF 8HP75 (Quadrifoglio) transmissions.\n36\t* https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maserati_Levante -- infobox states\n37\t  \"Platform: Chrysler LX platform\" (i.e. NOT the Giorgio platform the\n38\t  Stelvio/Grecale share); \"The Levante gains an eight speed ZF automatic\n39\t  transmission from the sixth generation Maserati Quattroporte.\"\n40\t* https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maserati_Ghibli_(M157) -- M157/Quattroporte\n41\t  VI-derived platform, same ZF 8HP-family transmission line as the Levante.\n42\t* https://www.go-parts.com/garage/wire-harness-trans-maserati-quattroporte-maserati-ghibli-maserati-levante-2014-2022\n43\t  -- names the Ghibli, Quattroporte and Levante as sharing the AWD\n44\t  transmission/harness (ZF 8HP70).\n45\t* https://www.go-parts.com/garage/transmission-assembly-alfa-romeo-giulia-alfa-romeo-stelvio-2017-2025\n46\t  -- Giulia/Stelvio 2.0L AWD use the ZF 8HP50, a different member of the\n47\t  same ZF 8HP transmission family, not an identical part.\n48\t* https://dot.report/wmi/ZN6 -- \"Maserati North America, Inc.\" holds WMI\n49\t  ``ZN6``, used for BOTH the Levante (2017-2024) and the Grecale\n50\t  (2023-present) -- no sourced way to tell the two models apart from the\n51\t  WMI alone.\n52\t\n53\tThe headline finding: **Grecale and Stelvio are genuine platform-mates**\n54\t(Giorgio platform, shared GME T4 2.0L engine family) -- a CORROBORATED,\n55\tsourced relationship. **Levante and Stelvio are NOT platform-mates** -- the\n56\tLevante's own Wikipedia infobox names the Chrysler LX platform, not\n57\tGiorgio -- so anything in common between a Levante and this Stelvio is\n58\tcomponent-level at best (the ZF 8HP transmission *family*, not the same\n59\tpart) and everything else is UNKNOWN rather than assumed.\n60\t\"\"\"\n61\t\n62\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n63\t\n64\timport re\n65\tfrom typing import Any, Optional\n66\t\n67\tCONFIRMED = \"CONFIRMED\"\n68\tCORROBORATED = \"CORROBORATED\"\n69\tSINGLE_SOURCE = \"SINGLE-SOURCE\"\n70\tUNKNOWN = \"UNKNOWN\"\n71\tCONFIDENCE_LEVELS = (CONFIRMED, CORROBORATED, SINGLE_SOURCE, UNKNOWN)\n72\t\n73\t#: ``shared_with`` model names this module recognises as \"sibling platform,\n74\t#: not this car\" -- the set ``mes.experience``/``mes.parts`` check an\n75\t#: entry's ``vehicle_fit``/``fits`` field against before tagging it with\n76\t#: ``sibling_of``.\n77\tSIBLING_MODELS = frozenset({\"grecale\", \"levante\"})\n78\t\n79\t\n80\tdef _share(model: str, what_is_shared: list[str], confidence: str,\n81\t           source: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n82\t    if confidence not in CONFIDENCE_LEVELS:\n83\t        raise ValueError(f\"bad confidence {confidence!r} for shared_with[{model!r}]\")\n84\t    if not source:\n85\t        raise ValueError(f\"shared_with[{model!r}] has no source\")\n86\t    return {\"model\": model, \"what_is_shared\": list(what_is_shared),\n87\t            \"confidence\": confidence, \"source\": source}\n88\t\n89\t\n90\t_WIKI_GRECALE = \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maserati_Grecale\"\n91\t_WIKI_GME = \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FCA_Global_Medium_Engine\"\n92\t_WIKI_STELVIO = \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfa_Romeo_Stelvio\"\n93\t_WIKI_GIULIA = \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfa_Romeo_Giulia_(2015)\"\n94\t_WIKI_LEVANTE = \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maserati_Levante\"\n95\t_WIKI_GHIBLI = \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maserati_Ghibli_(M157)\"\n96\t_GOPARTS_GIULIA_STELVIO_ZF = (\"https://www.go-parts.com/garage/transmission-assembly-\"\n97\t                               \"alfa-romeo-giulia-alfa-romeo-stelvio-2017-2025\")\n98\t_GOPARTS_MASERATI_ZF = (\"https://www.go-parts.com/garage/wire-harness-trans-maserati-\"\n99\t                          \"quattroporte-maserati-ghibli-maserati-levante-2014-2022\")\n100\t_DOT_REPORT_ZN6 = \"https://dot.report/wmi/ZN6\"\n101\t\n102\t_GIORGIO_PLATFORM_GME = [\n103\t    \"Giorgio platform (body structure, suspension architecture)\",\n104\t    \"GME T4 2.0L turbocharged inline-4 engine family\",\n105\t]\n106\t_NOT_PLATFORM_SHARED_ZF_ONLY = [\n107\t    \"ZF 8HP-family automatic transmission (different member of the family: \"\n108\t    \"this car's 2.0T uses a ZF 8HP50/8HP75; the Levante uses a ZF 8HP70 -- \"\n109\t    \"same supplier family, not an identical part). NOT a shared platform: \"\n110\t    \"Levante is built on the Chrysler LX platform per its own Wikipedia \"\n111\t    \"infobox, this car on Giorgio. Any other component overlap \"\n112\t    \"(suspension, electronics, suppliers) is UNKNOWN -- not checked this \"\n113\t    \"pass.\",\n114\t]\n115\t\n116\tPLATFORMS: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = {\n117\t    \"stelvio\": {\n118\t        \"platform\": \"FCA/Stellantis Giorgio platform\",\n119\t        \"years\": \"2017-present (2018 model year, this project's VIN)\",\n120\t        \"shared_with\": [\n121\t            _share(\"giulia\", _GIORGIO_PLATFORM_GME, CORROBORATED,\n122\t                   f\"{_WIKI_STELVIO} ; {_WIKI_GIULIA} ; {_WIKI_GME}\"),\n123\t            _share(\"grecale\", _GIORGIO_PLATFORM_GME, CORROBORATED,\n124\t                   f\"{_WIKI_GRECALE} (\\\"the Grecale shares the company's \"\n125\t                   f\"Giorgio platform with the Alfa Romeo Stelvio\\\") ; {_WIKI_GME}\"),\n126\t            _share(\"levante\", _NOT_PLATFORM_SHARED_ZF_ONLY, SINGLE_SOURCE,\n127\t                   f\"{_GOPARTS_GIULIA_STELVIO_ZF} ; {_WIKI_LEVANTE}\"),\n128\t        ],\n129\t    },\n130\t    \"giulia\": {\n131\t        \"platform\": \"FCA/Stellantis Giorgio platform\",\n132\t        \"years\": \"2015/2016-present\",\n133\t        \"shared_with\": [\n134\t            _share(\"stelvio\", _GIORGIO_PLATFORM_GME, CORROBORATED,\n135\t                   f\"{_WIKI_STELVIO} ; {_WIKI_GIULIA} ; {_WIKI_GME}\"),\n136\t            _share(\"grecale\", _GIORGIO_PLATFORM_GME, CORROBORATED,\n137\t                   f\"{_WIKI_GRECALE} ; {_WIKI_GME}\"),\n138\t            _share(\"levante\", _NOT_PLATFORM_SHARED_ZF_ONLY, SINGLE_SOURCE,\n139\t                   f\"{_GOPARTS_GIULIA_STELVIO_ZF} ; {_WIKI_LEVANTE}\"),\n140\t        ],\n141\t    },\n142\t    \"grecale\": {\n143\t        \"platform\": \"FCA/Stellantis Giorgio platform (Maserati execution)\",\n144\t        \"years\": \"2023-present\",\n145\t        \"shared_with\": [\n146\t            _share(\"stelvio\", _GIORGIO_PLATFORM_GME, CORROBORATED,\n147\t                   f\"{_WIKI_GRECALE} ; {_WIKI_GME}\"),\n148\t            _share(\"giulia\", _GIORGIO_PLATFORM_GME, CORROBORATED,\n149\t                   f\"{_WIKI_GRECALE} ; {_WIKI_GME}\"),\n150\t            _share(\"levante\", [\"no sourced platform or component overlap found \"\n151\t                                \"this pass -- Grecale (Giorgio) and Levante \"\n152\t                                \"(Chrysler LX) are different platforms; both \"\n153\t                                \"share WMI ZN6 as Maserati North America \"\n154\t                                \"products, which is a VIN-registration fact, \"\n155\t                                \"not a shared-parts fact\"],\n156\t                   UNKNOWN, f\"{_WIKI_GRECALE} ; {_WIKI_LEVANTE} ; {_DOT_REPORT_ZN6}\"),\n157\t        ],\n158\t    },\n159\t    \"levante\": {\n160\t        \"platform\": \"Chrysler LX platform (per Wikipedia's Levante infobox); \"\n161\t                     \"informally described in some coverage as sharing the \"\n162\t                     \"Ghibli/Quattroporte VI-era Maserati architecture, but \"\n163\t                     \"that specific platform-identity claim was not confirmed \"\n164\t                     \"against a primary source this pass -- treat as UNKNOWN, \"\n165\t                     \"not as the Giorgio platform this project's car uses.\",\n166\t        \"years\": \"2016-2024\",\n167\t        \"shared_with\": [\n168\t            _share(\"ghibli\", [\"ZF 8HP70 automatic transmission (same \"\n169\t                                \"transmission the Levante \\\"gains ... from \"\n170\t                                \"the sixth generation Maserati Quattroporte\\\"; \"\n171\t                                \"Ghibli, Quattroporte and Levante share this \"\n172\t                                \"line per the sourced parts-vendor page)\",\n173\t                                \"AWD transmission wiring harness (per sourced \"\n174\t                                \"parts-vendor page)\"],\n175\t                   CORROBORATED, f\"{_WIKI_LEVANTE} ; {_WIKI_GHIBLI} ; {_GOPARTS_MASERATI_ZF}\"),\n176\t            _share(\"stelvio\", _NOT_PLATFORM_SHARED_ZF_ONLY, SINGLE_SOURCE,\n177\t                   f\"{_GOPARTS_GIULIA_STELVIO_ZF} ; {_WIKI_LEVANTE}\"),\n178\t            _share(\"grecale\", [\"no sourced platform or component overlap found \"\n179\t                                \"this pass -- see grecale/levante entry above\"],\n180\t                   UNKNOWN, f\"{_WIKI_LEVANTE} ; {_WIKI_GRECALE} ; {_DOT_REPORT_ZN6}\"),\n181\t        ],\n182\t    },\n183\t    \"ghibli\": {\n184\t        \"platform\": \"Maserati M157 platform (Quattroporte VI-derived)\",\n185\t        \"years\": \"2013-present\",\n186\t        \"shared_with\": [\n187\t            _share(\"levante\", [\"ZF 8HP70 automatic transmission\", \"AWD \"\n188\t                                \"transmission wiring harness\"],\n189\t                   CORROBORATED, f\"{_WIKI_GHIBLI} ; {_WIKI_LEVANTE} ; {_GOPARTS_MASERATI_ZF}\"),\n190\t        ],\n191\t    },\n192\t}\n193\t\n194\tfor _model, _rec in PLATFORMS.items():\n195\t    for _s in _rec[\"shared_with\"]:\n196\t        if not _s.get(\"source\"):\n197\t            raise ValueError(f\"{_model} -> {_s['model']} has no source\")\n198\t\n199\t#: VIN prefix (WMI, the first 3 characters) this project's own car's VIN\n200\t#: starts with -- confirmed directly against the project VIN\n201\t#: ``ZASFAKPN5J7B88115`` (see project_stelvio_evap.md memory).\n202\t_WMI_STELVIO_RE = re.compile(r\"^ZASF\", re.IGNORECASE)\n203\t\n204\t#: WMI ``ZN6`` is held by \"Maserati North America, Inc.\" (sourced:\n205\t#: https://dot.report/wmi/ZN6) and is used for BOTH the Levante\n206\t#: (2017-2024) and the Grecale (2023-present) -- no sourced VIN position\n207\t#: was found this pass that reliably distinguishes the two models from the\n208\t#: WMI alone, so a VIN starting with this prefix resolves to UNKNOWN rather\n209\t#: than guessing which Maserati SUV it is. ``ZN7`` was searched for and no\n210\t#: source was found assigning it to any Maserati model -- also UNKNOWN.\n211\t_WMI_MASERATI_SUV_RE = re.compile(r\"^(ZN6|ZN7)\", re.IGNORECASE)\n212\t\n213\t\n214\tdef siblings(model: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n215\t    \"\"\"Sourced sibling-platform relationships for ``model`` (e.g.\n216\t    ``\"stelvio\"``). Each item: ``{model, shared, confidence, source}``.\n217\t    Returns ``[]`` for an unrecognised model -- never a guess.\n218\t    \"\"\"\n219\t    key = (model or \"\").strip().lower()\n220\t    rec = PLATFORMS.get(key)\n221\t    if rec is None:\n222\t        return []\n223\t    return [\n224\t        {\"model\": s[\"model\"], \"shared\": list(s[\"what_is_shared\"]),\n225\t         \"confidence\": s[\"confidence\"], \"source\": s[\"source\"]}\n226\t        for s in rec.get(\"shared_with\", [])\n227\t    ]\n228\t\n229\t\n230\tdef model_for_vin(vin: str) -> str:\n231\t    \"\"\"Best-effort model name from a VIN's WMI (first 3-4 characters).\n232\t\n233\t    Returns ``\"stelvio\"`` for this project's own car's VIN prefix, and\n234\t    ``\"UNKNOWN\"`` for anything not confidently sourced -- including a\n235\t    Maserati ``ZN6``/``ZN7`` WMI, which this research pass could not\n236\t    reliably split between Levante and Grecale (see module docstring).\n237\t    Never guesses a specific model from an ambiguous WMI.\n238\t    \"\"\"\n239\t    v = (vin or \"\").strip().upper()\n240\t    if not v:\n241\t        return UNKNOWN\n242\t    if _WMI_STELVIO_RE.match(v):\n243\t        return \"stelvio\"\n244\t    if _WMI_MASERATI_SUV_RE.match(v):\n245\t        return UNKNOWN\n246\t    return UNKNOWN\n247\t\n248\t\n249\tdef platform_for(model: str) -> Optional[dict[str, Any]]:\n250\t    \"\"\"The platform record for ``model``, or ``None`` if unrecognised.\"\"\"\n251\t    key = (model or \"\").strip().lower()\n252\t    rec = PLATFORMS.get(key)\n253\t    if rec is None:\n254\t        return None\n255\t    return {\"model\": key, \"platform\": rec[\"platform\"], \"years\": rec[\"years\"],\n256\t            \"shared_with\": siblings(key)}\n257\t\n258\t\n259\t__all__ = [\"CONFIRMED\", \"CORROBORATED\", \"SINGLE_SOURCE\", \"UNKNOWN\",\n260\t          \"CONFIDENCE_LEVELS\", \"SIBLING_MODELS\", \"PLATFORMS\",\n261\t          \"siblings\", \"model_for_vin\", \"platform_for\"]\n262\t"}]},"uuid":"b1caaa57-e894-4db1-b111-7f6e8554ee9c","timestamp":"2026-10-08T11:44:08.522Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\mes-log-mcp\\mes\\platform.py","content":"\"\"\"Platform relationships between this project's car and its \"similar\"\nStellantis/Maserati siblings.\n\nThe user has described the 2018 Alfa Romeo Stelvio 2.0T's two \"similar\"\nsibling cars as the Maserati Levante and the Maserati Grecale. House rule\n(see ``feedback_...`` memory): never present an unverified relationship as\nfact. This module is a small, sourced table of what is actually shared\nbetween these cars' platforms -- and, just as importantly, what is NOT --\nso the rest of the project (``mes.experience``, ``mes.parts``,\n``mes.code_feel`` and their ``cuore`` bridges) can label a sibling-platform\nresult \"verify fit\" instead of presenting it as settled.\n\nConfidence levels (never invented -- an absent/unverified relationship is\nrecorded as UNKNOWN, never guessed):\n\n* ``CONFIRMED``     -- stated directly by a primary source (the\n                       manufacturer's own platform article/spec sheet).\n* ``CORROBORATED``  -- two independent sources agree (e.g. Wikipedia's\n                       Grecale article plus the FCA Global Medium Engine\n                       article both naming the same shared engine family).\n* ``SINGLE_SOURCE``  -- exactly one source found, not cross-checked.\n* ``UNKNOWN``       -- nothing credible found, or the two cars are\n                       confirmed to NOT share the thing being asked about\n                       (e.g. Levante and Stelvio do not share a platform).\n\nResearch pass: 2026-10-07, via web search + page fetch of:\n\n* https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maserati_Grecale -- \"the Grecale shares the\n  company's Giorgio platform with the Alfa Romeo Stelvio and the fifth\n  generation Jeep Grand Cherokee.\"\n* https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FCA_Global_Medium_Engine -- the GME T4 2.0L\n  turbo engine family, first fitted to the Giulia/Stelvio, also used in the\n  Grecale.\n* https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfa_Romeo_Stelvio -- Giorgio platform,\n  ZF 8HP50 (base/Ti) / ZF 8HP75 (Quadrifoglio) transmissions.\n* https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maserati_Levante -- infobox states\n  \"Platform: Chrysler LX platform\" (i.e. NOT the Giorgio platform the\n  Stelvio/Grecale share); \"The Levante gains an eight speed ZF automatic\n  transmission from the sixth generation Maserati Quattroporte.\"\n* https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maserati_Ghibli_(M157) -- M157/Quattroporte\n  VI-derived platform, same ZF 8HP-family transmission line as the Levante.\n* https://www.go-parts.com/garage/wire-harness-trans-maserati-quattroporte-maserati-ghibli-maserati-levante-2014-2022\n  -- names the Ghibli, Quattroporte and Levante as sharing the AWD\n  transmission/harness (ZF 8HP70).\n* https://www.go-parts.com/garage/transmission-assembly-alfa-romeo-giulia-alfa-romeo-stelvio-2017-2025\n  -- Giulia/Stelvio 2.0L AWD use the ZF 8HP50, a different member of the\n  same ZF 8HP transmission family, not an identical part.\n* https://dot.report/wmi/ZN6 -- \"Maserati North America, Inc.\" holds WMI\n  ``ZN6``, used for BOTH the Levante (2017-2024) and the Grecale\n  (2023-present) -- no sourced way to tell the two models apart from the\n  WMI alone.\n\nThe headline finding: **Grecale and Stelvio are genuine platform-mates**\n(Giorgio platform, shared GME T4 2.0L engine family) -- a CORROBORATED,\nsourced relationship. **Levante and Stelvio are NOT platform-mates** -- the\nLevante's own Wikipedia infobox names the Chrysler LX platform, not\nGiorgio -- so anything in common between a Levante and this Stelvio is\ncomponent-level at best (the ZF 8HP transmission *family*, not the same\npart) and everything else is UNKNOWN rather than assumed.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport re\nfrom typing import Any, Optional\n\nCONFIRMED = \"CONFIRMED\"\nCORROBORATED = \"CORROBORATED\"\nSINGLE_SOURCE = \"SINGLE-SOURCE\"\nUNKNOWN = \"UNKNOWN\"\nCONFIDENCE_LEVELS = (CONFIRMED, CORROBORATED, SINGLE_SOURCE, UNKNOWN)\n\n#: ``shared_with`` model names this module recognises as \"sibling platform,\n#: not this car\" -- the set ``mes.experience``/``mes.parts`` check an\n#: entry's ``vehicle_fit``/``fits`` field against before tagging it with\n#: ``sibling_of``.\nSIBLING_MODELS = frozenset({\"grecale\", \"levante\"})\n\n\ndef _share(model: str, what_is_shared: list[str], confidence: str,\n           source: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    if confidence not in CONFIDENCE_LEVELS:\n        raise ValueError(f\"bad confidence {confidence!r} for shared_with[{model!r}]\")\n    if not source:\n        raise ValueError(f\"shared_with[{model!r}] has no source\")\n    return {\"model\": model, \"what_is_shared\": list(what_is_shared),\n            \"confidence\": confidence, \"source\": source}\n\n\n_WIKI_GRECALE = \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maserati_Grecale\"\n_WIKI_GME = \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FCA_Global_Medium_Engine\"\n_WIKI_STELVIO = \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfa_Romeo_Stelvio\"\n_WIKI_GIULIA = \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfa_Romeo_Giulia_(2015)\"\n_WIKI_LEVANTE = \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maserati_Levante\"\n_WIKI_GHIBLI = \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maserati_Ghibli_(M157)\"\n_GOPARTS_GIULIA_STELVIO_ZF = (\"https://www.go-parts.com/garage/transmission-assembly-\"\n                               \"alfa-romeo-giulia-alfa-romeo-stelvio-2017-2025\")\n_GOPARTS_MASERATI_ZF = (\"https://www.go-parts.com/garage/wire-harness-trans-maserati-\"\n                          \"quattroporte-maserati-ghibli-maserati-levante-2014-2022\")\n_DOT_REPORT_ZN6 = \"https://dot.report/wmi/ZN6\"\n\n_GIORGIO_PLATFORM_GME = [\n    \"Giorgio platform (body structure, suspension architecture)\",\n    \"GME T4 2.0L turbocharged inline-4 engine family\",\n]\n_NOT_PLATFORM_SHARED_ZF_ONLY = [\n    \"ZF 8HP-family automatic transmission (different member of the family: \"\n    \"this car's 2.0T uses a ZF 8HP50/8HP75; the Levante uses a ZF 8HP70 -- \"\n    \"same supplier family, not an identical part). NOT a shared platform: \"\n    \"Levante is built on the Chrysler LX platform per its own Wikipedia \"\n    \"infobox, this car on Giorgio. Any other component overlap \"\n    \"(suspension, electronics, suppliers) is UNKNOWN -- not checked this \"\n    \"pass.\",\n]\n\nPLATFORMS: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = {\n    \"stelvio\": {\n        \"platform\": \"FCA/Stellantis Giorgio platform\",\n        \"years\": \"2017-present (2018 model year, this project's VIN)\",\n        \"shared_with\": [\n            _share(\"giulia\", _GIORGIO_PLATFORM_GME, CORROBORATED,\n                   f\"{_WIKI_STELVIO} ; {_WIKI_GIULIA} ; {_WIKI_GME}\"),\n            _share(\"grecale\", _GIORGIO_PLATFORM_GME, CORROBORATED,\n                   f\"{_WIKI_GRECALE} (\\\"the Grecale shares the company's \"\n                   f\"Giorgio platform with the Alfa Romeo Stelvio\\\") ; {_WIKI_GME}\"),\n            _share(\"levante\", _NOT_PLATFORM_SHARED_ZF_ONLY, SINGLE_SOURCE,\n                   f\"{_GOPARTS_GIULIA_STELVIO_ZF} ; {_WIKI_LEVANTE}\"),\n        ],\n    },\n    \"giulia\": {\n        \"platform\": \"FCA/Stellantis Giorgio platform\",\n        \"years\": \"2015/2016-present\",\n        \"shared_with\": [\n            _share(\"stelvio\", _GIORGIO_PLATFORM_GME, CORROBORATED,\n                   f\"{_WIKI_STELVIO} ; {_WIKI_GIULIA} ; {_WIKI_GME}\"),\n            _share(\"grecale\", _GIORGIO_PLATFORM_GME, CORROBORATED,\n                   f\"{_WIKI_GRECALE} ; {_WIKI_GME}\"),\n            _share(\"levante\", _NOT_PLATFORM_SHARED_ZF_ONLY, SINGLE_SOURCE,\n                   f\"{_GOPARTS_GIULIA_STELVIO_ZF} ; {_WIKI_LEVANTE}\"),\n        ],\n    },\n    \"grecale\": {\n        \"platform\": \"FCA/Stellantis Giorgio platform (Maserati execution)\",\n        \"years\": \"2023-present\",\n        \"shared_with\": [\n            _share(\"stelvio\", _GIORGIO_PLATFORM_GME, CORROBORATED,\n                   f\"{_WIKI_GRECALE} ; {_WIKI_GME}\"),\n            _share(\"giulia\", _GIORGIO_PLATFORM_GME, CORROBORATED,\n                   f\"{_WIKI_GRECALE} ; {_WIKI_GME}\"),\n            _share(\"levante\", [\"no sourced platform or component overlap found \"\n                                \"this pass -- Grecale (Giorgio) and Levante \"\n                                \"(Chrysler LX) are different platforms; both \"\n                                \"share WMI ZN6 as Maserati North America \"\n                                \"products, which is a VIN-registration fact, \"\n                                \"not a shared-parts fact\"],\n                   UNKNOWN, f\"{_WIKI_GRECALE} ; {_WIKI_LEVANTE} ; {_DOT_REPORT_ZN6}\"),\n        ],\n    },\n    \"levante\": {\n        \"platform\": \"Chrysler LX platform (per Wikipedia's Levante infobox); \"\n                     \"informally described in some coverage as sharing the \"\n                     \"Ghibli/Quattroporte VI-era Maserati architecture, but \"\n                     \"that specific platform-identity claim was not confirmed \"\n                     \"against a primary source this pass -- treat as UNKNOWN, \"\n                     \"not as the Giorgio platform this project's car uses.\",\n        \"years\": \"2016-2024\",\n        \"shared_with\": [\n            _share(\"ghibli\", [\"ZF 8HP70 automatic transmission (same \"\n                                \"transmission the Levante \\\"gains ... from \"\n                                \"the sixth generation Maserati Quattroporte\\\"; \"\n                                \"Ghibli, Quattroporte and Levante share this \"\n                                \"line per the sourced parts-vendor page)\",\n                                \"AWD transmission wiring harness (per sourced \"\n                                \"parts-vendor page)\"],\n                   CORROBORATED, f\"{_WIKI_LEVANTE} ; {_WIKI_GHIBLI} ; {_GOPARTS_MASERATI_ZF}\"),\n            _share(\"stelvio\", _NOT_PLATFORM_SHARED_ZF_ONLY, SINGLE_SOURCE,\n                   f\"{_GOPARTS_GIULIA_STELVIO_ZF} ; {_WIKI_LEVANTE}\"),\n            _share(\"grecale\", [\"no sourced platform or component overlap found \"\n                                \"this pass -- see grecale/levante entry above\"],\n                   UNKNOWN, f\"{_WIKI_LEVANTE} ; {_WIKI_GRECALE} ; {_DOT_REPORT_ZN6}\"),\n        ],\n    },\n    \"ghibli\": {\n        \"platform\": \"Maserati M157 platform (Quattroporte VI-derived)\",\n        \"years\": \"2013-present\",\n        \"shared_with\": [\n            _share(\"levante\", [\"ZF 8HP70 automatic transmission\", \"AWD \"\n                                \"transmission wiring harness\"],\n                   CORROBORATED, f\"{_WIKI_GHIBLI} ; {_WIKI_LEVANTE} ; {_GOPARTS_MASERATI_ZF}\"),\n        ],\n    },\n}\n\nfor _model, _rec in PLATFORMS.items():\n    for _s in _rec[\"shared_with\"]:\n        if not _s.get(\"source\"):\n            raise ValueError(f\"{_model} -> {_s['model']} has no source\")\n\n#: VIN prefix (WMI, the first 3 characters) this project's own car's VIN\n#: starts with -- confirmed directly against the project VIN\n#: ``ZASFAKPN5J7B88115`` (see project_stelvio_evap.md memory).\n_WMI_STELVIO_RE = re.compile(r\"^ZASF\", re.IGNORECASE)\n\n#: WMI ``ZN6`` is held by \"Maserati North America, Inc.\" (sourced:\n#: https://dot.report/wmi/ZN6) and is used for BOTH the Levante\n#: (2017-2024) and the Grecale (2023-present) -- no sourced VIN position\n#: was found this pass that reliably distinguishes the two models from the\n#: WMI alone, so a VIN starting with this prefix resolves to UNKNOWN rather\n#: than guessing which Maserati SUV it is. ``ZN7`` was searched for and no\n#: source was found assigning it to any Maserati model -- also UNKNOWN.\n_WMI_MASERATI_SUV_RE = re.compile(r\"^(ZN6|ZN7)\", re.IGNORECASE)\n\n\ndef siblings(model: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Sourced sibling-platform relationships for ``model`` (e.g.\n    ``\"stelvio\"``). Each item: ``{model, shared, confidence, source}``.\n    Returns ``[]`` for an unrecognised model -- never a guess.\n    \"\"\"\n    key = (model or \"\").strip().lower()\n    rec = PLATFORMS.get(key)\n    if rec is None:\n        return []\n    return [\n        {\"model\": s[\"model\"], \"shared\": list(s[\"what_is_shared\"]),\n         \"confidence\": s[\"confidence\"], \"source\": s[\"source\"]}\n        for s in rec.get(\"shared_with\", [])\n    ]\n\n\ndef model_for_vin(vin: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Best-effort model name from a VIN's WMI (first 3-4 characters).\n\n    Returns ``\"stelvio\"`` for this project's own car's VIN prefix, and\n    ``\"UNKNOWN\"`` for anything not confidently sourced -- including a\n    Maserati ``ZN6``/``ZN7`` WMI, which this research pass could not\n    reliably split between Levante and Grecale (see module docstring).\n    Never guesses a specific model from an ambiguous WMI.\n    \"\"\"\n    v = (vin or \"\").strip().upper()\n    if not v:\n        return UNKNOWN\n    if _WMI_STELVIO_RE.match(v):\n        return \"stelvio\"\n    if _WMI_MASERATI_SUV_RE.match(v):\n        return UNKNOWN\n    return UNKNOWN\n\n\ndef platform_for(model: str) -> Optional[dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"The platform record for ``model``, or ``None`` if unrecognised.\"\"\"\n    key = (model or \"\").strip().lower()\n    rec = PLATFORMS.get(key)\n    if rec is None:\n        return None\n    return {\"model\": key, \"platform\": rec[\"platform\"], \"years\": rec[\"years\"],\n            \"shared_with\": siblings(key)}\n\n\n__all__ = [\"CONFIRMED\", \"CORROBORATED\", \"SINGLE_SOURCE\", \"UNKNOWN\",\n          \"CONFIDENCE_LEVELS\", \"SIBLING_MODELS\", \"PLATFORMS\",\n          \"siblings\", \"model_for_vin\", \"platform_for\"]\n","numLines":262,"startLine":1,"totalLines":262}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9efdfdf4-685d-475b-8aa9-7f640e7535cf","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
