{"parentUuid":"bc6cb473-588b-4671-9ce2-675154682327","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"daebc1ae-8924-401f-8c9a-2ac46dcface0","agentId":"acbfb63ee5bb37cdd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XWXB7VCy3K7Ky1L3o6DcBj","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{# Reusable \"Others' experience\" card: links other owners/forums/videos have\n2\t   published about a code, family or job. Fed by the `experience_links`\n3\t   Jinja global (registered as an import-time side effect by\n4\t   cuore/web/experience_globals.py -- see that module's docstring) via a\n5\t   page-local `exp = experience_links(...)` set before this include.\n6\t   Guarded so a page still renders -- with the empty state below -- before\n7\t   that global lands, and before mes.experience itself lands.\n8\t\n9\t   Collapsed by default (<details class=\"card-details\">, no `open`) so the\n10\t   card doesn't crowd the page; the summary names the count and teases the\n11\t   top-scored link. Inside, four view links (?exp=relevant|videos|forums|\n12\t   newest) re-render the already-scored list filtered/sorted without any\n13\t   JS -- `request` is only defined when a route passes it into the\n14\t   template context (it always does via `TemplateResponse(request, ...)`),\n15\t   so this degrades to the default \"relevant\" view if it isn't. #}\n16\t{% set exp = exp if exp is defined else {\"links\": [], \"count\": 0} %}\n17\t{% set _exp_mode = (request.query_params.get('exp') if request is defined and request else none) or \"relevant\" %}\n18\t\n19\t{% set _exp_kind_icon = {\n20\t  \"how_to_video\": \"[video]\",\n21\t  \"teardown\": \"[teardown]\",\n22\t  \"forum_thread\": \"[forum]\",\n23\t  \"owner_report\": \"[report]\",\n24\t  \"sound_reference\": \"[sound]\"\n25\t} %}\n26\t\n27\t{% if _exp_mode == \"videos\" %}\n28\t  {% set _exp_shown = exp.links|selectattr(\"kind\", \"equalto\", \"how_to_video\")|list %}\n29\t{% elif _exp_mode == \"forums\" %}\n30\t  {% set _exp_shown = exp.links|selectattr(\"kind\", \"equalto\", \"forum_thread\")|list %}\n31\t{% elif _exp_mode == \"newest\" %}\n32\t  {% set _exp_shown = exp.links|sort(attribute=\"date\", reverse=true)|list %}\n33\t{% else %}\n34\t  {% set _exp_shown = exp.links %}\n35\t{% endif %}\n36\t\n37\t<div class=\"panel experience-card\">\n38\t  {% if not exp.links %}\n39\t  <h3>Others' experience</h3>\n40\t  <p class=\"muted small\">No experience links yet for this item.</p>\n41\t  {% else %}\n42\t  <details class=\"card-details\">\n43\t    <summary>Others' experience ({{ exp.count }}) &mdash; {{ exp.links[0].title }}</summary>\n44\t    <p class=\"small muted exp-views\">\n45\t      view:\n46\t      <a href=\"?exp=relevant\">relevant</a> &middot;\n47\t      <a href=\"?exp=videos\">videos</a> &middot;\n48\t      <a href=\"?exp=forums\">forums</a> &middot;\n49\t      <a href=\"?exp=newest\">newest</a>\n50\t    </p>\n51\t    {% for l in _exp_shown %}\n52\t      <div class=\"exp-row\">\n53\t        <span class=\"small muted\">#{{ loop.index }}</span>\n54\t        <span class=\"small\">{{ _exp_kind_icon.get(l.kind, \"[link]\") }}</span>\n55\t        <div class=\"exp-main\">\n56\t          <a href=\"{{ l.url }}\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">{{ l.title }}</a>\n57\t          <div class=\"small muted\">{{ l.source }}{% if l.date %} &middot; {{ l.date }}{% endif %}</div>\n58\t          {% if l.reason %}<div class=\"small muted\">{{ l.reason }}</div>{% endif %}\n59\t          {% if l.label %}<div class=\"small muted\">{{ l.label }}</div>{% endif %}\n60\t        </div>\n61\t        {% if l.reputation %}<span class=\"chip {{ 'ok' if l.reputation == 'high' else 'plain' }}\">{{ l.reputation }}</span>{% endif %}\n62\t      </div>\n63\t    {% else %}\n64\t      <p class=\"muted small\">No links for this view.</p>\n65\t    {% endfor %}\n66\t  </details>\n67\t  {% endif %}\n68\t</div>\n69\t"}]},"uuid":"47e76f62-95f6-4817-a9c3-d7ddadc4eb01","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:00:51.620Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\web\\templates\\_experience.html","content":"{# Reusable \"Others' experience\" card: links other owners/forums/videos have\n   published about a code, family or job. Fed by the `experience_links`\n   Jinja global (registered as an import-time side effect by\n   cuore/web/experience_globals.py -- see that module's docstring) via a\n   page-local `exp = experience_links(...)` set before this include.\n   Guarded so a page still renders -- with the empty state below -- before\n   that global lands, and before mes.experience itself lands.\n\n   Collapsed by default (<details class=\"card-details\">, no `open`) so the\n   card doesn't crowd the page; the summary names the count and teases the\n   top-scored link. Inside, four view links (?exp=relevant|videos|forums|\n   newest) re-render the already-scored list filtered/sorted without any\n   JS -- `request` is only defined when a route passes it into the\n   template context (it always does via `TemplateResponse(request, ...)`),\n   so this degrades to the default \"relevant\" view if it isn't. #}\n{% set exp = exp if exp is defined else {\"links\": [], \"count\": 0} %}\n{% set _exp_mode = (request.query_params.get('exp') if request is defined and request else none) or \"relevant\" %}\n\n{% set _exp_kind_icon = {\n  \"how_to_video\": \"[video]\",\n  \"teardown\": \"[teardown]\",\n  \"forum_thread\": \"[forum]\",\n  \"owner_report\": \"[report]\",\n  \"sound_reference\": \"[sound]\"\n} %}\n\n{% if _exp_mode == \"videos\" %}\n  {% set _exp_shown = exp.links|selectattr(\"kind\", \"equalto\", \"how_to_video\")|list %}\n{% elif _exp_mode == \"forums\" %}\n  {% set _exp_shown = exp.links|selectattr(\"kind\", \"equalto\", \"forum_thread\")|list %}\n{% elif _exp_mode == \"newest\" %}\n  {% set _exp_shown = exp.links|sort(attribute=\"date\", reverse=true)|list %}\n{% else %}\n  {% set _exp_shown = exp.links %}\n{% endif %}\n\n<div class=\"panel experience-card\">\n  {% if not exp.links %}\n  <h3>Others' experience</h3>\n  <p class=\"muted small\">No experience links yet for this item.</p>\n  {% else %}\n  <details class=\"card-details\">\n    <summary>Others' experience ({{ exp.count }}) &mdash; {{ exp.links[0].title }}</summary>\n    <p class=\"small muted exp-views\">\n      view:\n      <a href=\"?exp=relevant\">relevant</a> &middot;\n      <a href=\"?exp=videos\">videos</a> &middot;\n      <a href=\"?exp=forums\">forums</a> &middot;\n      <a href=\"?exp=newest\">newest</a>\n    </p>\n    {% for l in _exp_shown %}\n      <div class=\"exp-row\">\n        <span class=\"small muted\">#{{ loop.index }}</span>\n        <span class=\"small\">{{ _exp_kind_icon.get(l.kind, \"[link]\") }}</span>\n        <div class=\"exp-main\">\n          <a href=\"{{ l.url }}\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">{{ l.title }}</a>\n          <div class=\"small muted\">{{ l.source }}{% if l.date %} &middot; {{ l.date }}{% endif %}</div>\n          {% if l.reason %}<div class=\"small muted\">{{ l.reason }}</div>{% endif %}\n          {% if l.label %}<div class=\"small muted\">{{ l.label }}</div>{% endif %}\n        </div>\n        {% if l.reputation %}<span class=\"chip {{ 'ok' if l.reputation == 'high' else 'plain' }}\">{{ l.reputation }}</span>{% endif %}\n      </div>\n    {% else %}\n      <p class=\"muted small\">No links for this view.</p>\n    {% endfor %}\n  </details>\n  {% endif %}\n</div>\n","numLines":69,"startLine":1,"totalLines":69}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bc6cb473-588b-4671-9ce2-675154682327","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"47e76f62-95f6-4817-a9c3-d7ddadc4eb01","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"acbfb63ee5bb37cdd","attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14884060 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"fe176d15-5e09-421d-8591-2d02f161dd87","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:00:51.644Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14884060 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"fe176d15-5e09-421d-8591-2d02f161dd87","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"acbfb63ee5bb37cdd","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfpjWrBxNgSFiJPoPtmZZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JkvpwbCSGCrSzV3sLw8Def","name":"SubagentHandback","input":{"message":"Done. 26/26 checks pass (`.venv/Scripts/python.exe cuore/tests/check_experience_page.py` exits 0).\n\nFiles changed:\n- cuore/services/experience_bridge.py — links_for() now scores each link (relevance by match type: code 100/family 60/job 40, +vehicle_fit bonus exact 30/sibling 10 via mes.platform.model_for_vin+siblings; importance: reputation high 20/medium 10, kind how_to_video 15/teardown 12/forum_thread 10/sound_reference 8/owner_report 5, recency +1/yr since 2020 capped 6), dedupes keeping the max-scoring instance of each link, sorts descending by score, and adds a `reason` string (e.g. \"exact code, this model, hands-on video\") plus the existing `sibling_of` label logic.\n- cuore/web/templates/_experience.html — non-empty results render inside a collapsed `<details class=\"card-details\">` (summary: \"Others' experience (N) — <top link title>\"); empty results keep the old always-visible \"Others' experience\" heading + empty-state text (needed so pre-existing per-item checks on maintenance.html, which has many items with no job match, still find the heading). Inside the details, view links `?exp=relevant|videos|forums|newest` filter/sort `exp.links` via `request.query_params.get('exp')` (falls back to \"relevant\" if `request` isn't defined). Each row shows rank #, a plain-text kind tag ([video]/[teardown]/[forum]/[report]/[sound]), title (external, rel=noopener), source/date, the `reason` in small muted text, and a reputation chip. Reused only existing CSS classes (card-details, chip, small, muted) — cuore.css untouched.\n- cuore/tests/check_experience_page.py — added 3 checks: scores descending + exact-code video first; card collapsed by default with \"(3)\" in the summary on the code page; ?exp=forums hides the video's own link (checked by href, since the summary teaser always names the top-scored link regardless of filter — that's intentional per spec).\n\nNote: mes.experience already exists in this environment with real curated data for P0456 (landed 2026-10-07 per the test's own comment), so some checks exercise real data, not just the fixture."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1597,"cache_read_input_tokens":115837,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1597,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":26,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01JkvpwbCSGCrSzV3sLw8Def":{"message":"Done. 26/26 checks pass (`.venv/Scripts/python.exe cuore/tests/check_experience_page.py` exits 0).\n\nFiles changed:\n- cuore/services/experience_bridge.py — links_for() now scores each link (relevance by match type: code 100/family 60/job 40, +vehicle_fit bonus exact 30/sibling 10 via mes.platform.model_for_vin+siblings; importance: reputation high 20/medium 10, kind how_to_video 15/teardown 12/forum_thread 10/sound_reference 8/owner_report 5, recency +1/yr since 2020 capped 6), dedupes keeping the max-scoring instance of each link, sorts descending by score, and adds a `reason` string (e.g. \"exact code, this model, hands-on video\") plus the existing `sibling_of` label logic.\n- cuore/web/templates/_experience.html — non-empty results render inside a collapsed `<details class=\"card-details\">` (summary: \"Others' experience (N) — <top link title>\"); empty results keep the old always-visible \"Others' experience\" heading + empty-state text (needed so pre-existing per-item checks on maintenance.html, which has many items with no job match, still find the heading). Inside the details, view links `?exp=relevant|videos|forums|newest` filter/sort `exp.links` via `request.query_params.get('exp')` (falls back to \"relevant\" if `request` isn't defined). Each row shows rank #, a plain-text kind tag ([video]/[teardown]/[forum]/[report]/[sound]), title (external, rel=noopener), source/date, the `reason` in small muted text, and a reputation chip. Reused only existing CSS classes (card-details, chip, small, muted) — cuore.css untouched.\n- cuore/tests/check_experience_page.py — added 3 checks: scores descending + exact-code video first; card collapsed by default with \"(3)\" in the summary on the code page; ?exp=forums hides the video's own link (checked by href, since the summary teaser always names the top-scored link regardless of filter — that's intentional per spec).\n\nNote: mes.experience already exists in this environment with real curated data for P0456 (landed 2026-10-07 per the test's own comment), so some checks exercise real data, not just the fixture."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"a51dac67-13b5-406d-9f6f-7395fd91559a","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfpjWqwKZ8yFu5k4ovBbN","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"f5a8049d-9fd1-4d71-beb1-6265151c3e0b","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:01:03.737Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
